# Obeka, Splitter of Seconds has menace (CR 702.111b: one Memnite alone can not block it) and deals combat damage to creatures too, but the trigger wants combat damage to a player
# (CR 510.2): two Memnites double-block it, no damage goes to Bot2 (20) and the second main phase follows the end of combat
# directly, with no additional upkeep step. The unblocked attack in the first scenario is the positive control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Obeka, Splitter of Seconds
Island
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Memnite
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Obeka, Splitter of Seconds.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Obeka, Splitter of Seconds)
! Bot2.Block(Memnite#1 > Obeka, Splitter of Seconds)
Bot2.Block(Memnite#1 > Obeka, Splitter of Seconds; Memnite#2 > Obeka, Splitter of Seconds)
[T3 Bot1.EndCombat]
? Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Step = Main2

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
